  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>La Barque Bleue is a seafood brasserie at 7 quai des Deux Emmanuels on the harbour of Nice, open since 1982 according to its official website. The menu features mussels, the catch of the day (sea bass, sardines, oysters), Italian-style pasta, pinsa and burgers; the tourist office also lists gluten-free dishes. The restaurant seats 110, including 50 on the terrace, with an indoor room heated in winter and air-conditioned in summer.</p>

      <h2>Dogs on site</h2>
      <p>The Nice Côte d'Azur tourist office, which lists the restaurant among its "Pet Friendly Nice Côte d'Azur" labelled venues, quotes the restaurant: "we have always spontaneously welcomed our animal friends and now, thanks to the Pet Friendly label, it's official! You will have a place for them, a bowl of water and even a small snack if they are hungry." The page does not say whether that place is indoors or on the terrace, and mentions no size or breed limit and no supplement. The restaurant's own website does not mention animals.</p>

      <h2>Hours and access</h2>
      <p>Open every day: non-stop service from 9:30 am to 10:30 pm (last service) according to the official website, breakfast from 9:30 am then continuous kitchen until 10 pm according to the tourist office. Parking, coach parking and wifi are listed. Phone: 04 93 55 39 74.</p>

      <h2>To check before you go</h2>
      <p>Where the dog may sit (indoor room or terrace) and the time of the last service (10 pm or 10:30 pm depending on the source): ask on 04 93 55 39 74.</p>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The restaurant faces the harbour of Nice, on the quay where the colourful pointu boats are moored (official website), for a walk with the dog before or after the meal.</p>

      <h2>Sources</h2>
      <p>Nice Côte d'Azur tourist office, restaurant-la-barque-bleue.fr, Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur Tourism: read on 15/11/2026.</p>
